Subject: [PATCH] Allow DHCP leases behind Wi-Fi AP proxy ARP

An AP can answer ARP announcements with the leased station address and the
AP MAC. Full address-conflict detection then declines the valid DHCP lease.
Keep the normal DHCP bind path and disable its ACD check on the ESP ports.

--- a/rtemslwip/esp32c3/lwipbspopts.h
+++ b/rtemslwip/esp32c3/lwipbspopts.h
@@ -113,4 +113,7 @@
  */
 #define LWIP_NETIF_STATUS_CALLBACK  1
 
+/* Wi-Fi AP proxy ARP can claim a station address with the AP MAC. */
+#define LWIP_DHCP_DOES_ACD_CHECK 0
+
 #endif /* RTEMSLWIP_ESP32C3_LWIPBSPOPTS_H */
--- a/rtemslwip/esp32c5/lwipbspopts.h
+++ b/rtemslwip/esp32c5/lwipbspopts.h
@@ -46,4 +46,7 @@
 
